It took me a lot of tries to ascend a zen ranger. Elven rangers are
pretty weak and I tend to play all roles as a fighter. Like always,
playing zen made me learn a bit more, and when I finally started to
play as suposed I started to make progress. It is of note how much
that was more important than early altars. Another factor in the
number of deaths was the long period in which I didn't play nethack
and had to re-learn lessons the hard way.

I started by naming my elven dagger Sting mostly to detect orcs, but
while I had +0 arrows I was wielding my bow and practicing it. I only
shot +2 arrows on more serious situations, and when I found new stacks
of arrows I also used them for practice.
I also used prayer to boost my max HP, and at level 2 it took me from
24 to 29 HP, which made a difference.

At Dlv 3 (after getting telepathy) I found a +2 splint mail and also a
lawful altar but since I wanted to get Stormbringer I first had to
create Orcrist so I left that altar aside for a while.

Minetown had a stethoscope, a magic harp (never used), a general shop
for price id and a co-aligned altar, but I still couldn't sac for
gifts. Sokoban was BoH version, and after getting the BoH I finally
got a runed broadsword from an elf. Now I could sac for stormbringer.

[part of story missing since ttyrec is corrupt; NAO had a problem and
I lost connection; the ttyrec is 16M so maybe there is a way to
recover it.]
During that time I had my monkey incident. I was using the travel
command to cross for nth-time the oracle level and was interrupted by
the monkey stealing me. Didn't even have a chance.
I think I also found a couple of magic lamps, using one for C?oGeno to
reverse geno silver dragons and get the scales. The second one I would
later use it for a magic marker, and since I had identified
?oCharging, I could genocide h and L.

Scorpius was easy since I burnt e-word on upstairs, and from his
throne I got a wish: blessed fixed +2 cloak of magic resistance.

Since I had identified both rings of teleportation and teleport
control I used them both and started eating tengus, getting lucky with
an early corpse.
The rest of the game was mostly uneventful, apart for a few dangerous
situations. Expert bow skill and teleport at will saved the situation
a few times.

As for the ascension run it also went smoothly: being chaotic meant
few misterious force events and the planes also were quick. Even the
water plane could have been worse: despite searching the portal for
quite some time (~500 turns) rodney didn't appear. I was expecting the
/oSecretDoorDetection would detect it but apparently it didn't work
for some reason.

I started the Astral plane with 300 HP -37 AC and some heavily
enchanted weaponry, so I was maybe a little overconfident. I went
first for Pestilence altar, and it was a wrong one. On the way back I
decided to melee Pestilence (my arrows were poisoned) with stormy and
tame it just for fun. However, I had to use a lot of !oFH and decided
instead to just run away for the next altar.
Death got me on my way to Famine, so I decided to try that altar
instead. Death took me from max 331HP to max 208 HP, so it was a Good
Thing that was the right altar.

